236134,"","C","2026-07-29","2026-09-15",1,0,0,"","FT"],[236875,"","SP","2026-07-31","2026-09-15",1,0,0,"","FT"],[236915,"","C","2026-07-31","2026-08-27",1,0,0,"","FT"],[236938,"","F","2026-08-04","2026-08-31",1,0,0,"","FT"],[238389,"","C","2026-08-04","2026-08-14",1,0,0,"","FT"],[241601,"","C","2026-08-11","2026-08-27",1,0,0,"","FT"],[242456,"","F","2026-08-13","2026-09-18",1,0,0,"","RN"],[243032,"","F","2026-08-14","2026-08-27",1,0,0,"","FT"],[243939,"","F","2026-08-18","2026-08-27",1,0,0,"","FT"],[244477,"","F","2026-08-18","2026-09-01",1,0,0,"","R1"],[245281,"","F","2026-08-19","2026-09-01",1,0,0,"","FT"],[247154,"","LLP","2026-08-27",null,1,0,0,"","FT"],[247934,"","SP","2026-08-24","2026-09-09",1,0,0,"","FT"],[250508,"","SP","2026-08-29",null,1,0,0,"","FT"],[250871,"","SP","2026-08-30",null,1,0,0,"","FT"],[251203,"","SP","2026-08-31","2026-09-03",1,0,0,"","FT"],[251448,"","F","2026-08-31",null,1,0,0,"","FT"],[252721,"","F","2026-09-02",null,1,0,0,"","FT"],[252892,"","C",null,null,1,0,0,"","FT"],[253146,"","SP","2026-09-03","2026-09-09",1,0,0,"","FT"],[254119,"","SP","2026-09-07",null,1,0,0,"","FT"],[254807,"","F","2026-09-17",null,1,0,0,"","FT"],[255108,"","LLP","2026-09-08",null,1,0,0,"","FT"],[256195,"","F","2026-09-08","2026-09-22",1,0,0,"","FT"],[259711,"","C","2026-09-15",null,1,0,0,"","FT"]],"notes":{"qualityHeader":"Referees deduped to their first referral, 38679 and internal ids excluded. Aug vs Sept 1 to 23, flagged referrer 85276 excluded. Money in USD at the Sept median rate of ₹95 per dollar.","qualityWindow":"Activation is measured on a 10-day window because the campaign is 17 days old; the usual 17 to 19 day median means most campaign referees have not had time to activate yet. Read the last two columns as early signal, not a result.","refereeQuality":["Referees from single-signup referrers look as good as August's, slightly better on value. 53% onboard in a day vs 55%, 18% activate within 10 days vs 16%, and the median first settlement is $2,146 vs $1,867.","Referees from 2+ signup referrers are a different population. 36% onboard in a day and 44% in a week, against 65% in August. Their median first settlement is $309, about a sixth of the norm. The few who activate do so quickly (22% within 10 days), but the stream is mostly noise: 312 signups, 77 old enough to judge. The 120 signups from the flagged referrer would have made this far worse and are left out.","The mix has moved toward freelancers, 58% of Sept onboardings vs 49% in Aug, with companies down from 12% to 10%. The company referees Sept does bring are activating better than August's, 15% within 10 days vs 8%, though that is 20 people.","Stated monthly volume is unchanged where it matters. Referees stating $10K or more are 4.4% of Aug onboardings and 4.7% of Sept. More Sept referees fill in the field at all (62% vs 54%), and nearly all of the extra answers are under $10K. None of the Sept $10K+ referees has activated yet, which is worth watching since these were the ones Sales would chase.","Net: the campaign is not lowering the quality of a referral from a normal referrer. It is adding a second stream of low-intent signups from people chasing the higher rungs, and that stream should be judged separately rather than averaged in."],"referrers":["478 people have referred on the campaign, excluding the flagged referrer 85276. 397 of them (83%) sent exactly one signup, and those convert to onboarding at 61%. The other 81 sent 317 signups between them, 44% of the total, but only 141 onboarded (45%) and 30 activated. Volume and ladder progress are not the same thing: the top ten senders produced 123 signups, 48 onboardings and 15 activations, and exporter 38154's 35 signups have yielded 6 onboardings and 1 activation.","The healthiest cohort is repeat referrers with 1-2 prior achievements. 87 people, 1.6 signups each, 57% onboarding, 23 activations. They go a little deeper than first-timers without the dilution. Past power referrers (3+ achieved) send 2.6 each but only 45% onboard. First-timers are the largest group at 299 (63%) and convert normally at 54%.","172 referrers (36%) have zero onboarded referees against 212 signups. That is the cheapest recovery pool in the campaign: the referrer already made the ask, the referee already signed up, someone just needs to finish the form.","89 referrers (19%) have never activated on Skydo themselves. They brought 122 signups, 63 onboarded, 5 activated. 39 onboarded in September and referred within days. The ladder is being promoted by people who have not used the product, which explains some of the weaker referee quality.","Onboarding rates are now similar across business types, 52 to 55%. Tenure is spread evenly: 148 referrers activated in the last three months, 103 over a year ago.","70 have unlocked at least the Polaroid. 19 have claimed it. The 51 who have not are still on the ladder, including the two people above AirPods."],"excluded":"Excluded from every campaign number on this page: exporter 85276 (freelancer, onboarded May 2025, never transacted). 120 signups, 119 of them between 02:47 and 09:54 IST on 24 Sep, one every 56 seconds on median. 115 distinct phone numbers, so these look like real people, but 83 never picked a business type and 2 have onboarded. The pattern fits a link posted into a large group rather than personal referrals. Left in, it would push signups to 833, signups per referrer to 1.74 and first-timer onboarding to 43%. Onboardings are barely affected. Worth an Ops review before any of these referees activate.","cohorts":"The lift on the activated base dipped to +13% at day 21 as Aug's deadline week kicked in, and is back to +22% at day 23 after a strong 22 and 23 Sep. Past referrers (1b, +56%) and recently dormant users (1.2, +35%) carry it. Never-referrers (1a) are at 1.07% vs 1.05%, essentially level with Aug: the campaign has reached about as many first-time referrers as the Tommy trolley did at this point, not more.","mix":"63% of campaign referrers have never referred before, but first-timers are only level with Aug on a like-for-like basis; the referrer increase is mostly repeats. Past power referrers (3+) bring 2.6 signups each and only 45% onboard, so they are sharing wider and shallower.","weeklyQuality":"Across all referrals (38679 excluded) Sept 1-day onboarding is running below the 52 to 56% of Mar to Aug. The gap sits with referrers sending 2+ signups: single-signup senders convert at 53%, people sending 7+ at 18%. Self-referrals are 6% of signups vs 11 to 12% in Jun to Aug. The 14 Sep week is still filling in.","claims":"19 of 70 people who unlocked a reward have claimed it, all at the Polaroid rung and all at exactly one activation. The two referrers above AirPods have not claimed, which is the behaviour the ladder was designed for.","popupHeader":"Mixpanel, Sept 1-23. Every event so far is at the first rung.","popup":["Still nobody has pressed keep referring. Eighteen took the camera, six closed the popup without choosing. At the first rung the trade is a camera already earned against two more activations at 17 to 19 days each, and for most people that is a bad bet.","One of those who backed out kept referring anyway and is now one activation from AirPods, so the zero measures button presses rather than intent. Worth checking with Tech whether that button changes any state."],"pace":"Projection takes the share of the month that days 1 to 23 delivered in Jun, Jul and Aug (74%, 73%, 71%) and applies it to 419. Straight line run rate gives 547. Week 1 brought 143 onboardings, week 2 brought 103, week 3 brought 117, and 22 to 23 Sep brought 50. Aug reached 327 by this point and closed at 462, but Aug had a 31 Aug deadline that pulled its last week forward; Sept has no deadline, so read the projection as a ceiling and the straight line as a floor. 552 sits between the two, so it needs the last seven days to run slightly above the month average. 600 needs about 26 a day for the last seven days against a run rate of 18.","daily":"7-day average line. Week 1 signups 243, week 2 162, week 3 205. 22 Sep: 60 signups from 46 referrers, the best day of the campaign. Today is not charted until the day is complete.","ladder":"269 onboarded referees belong to people who have not unlocked anything yet. At the usual 70 to 75% activation rate that is roughly 194 more Polaroids in the pipeline. Exporter 133487 has unlocked Ray-Ban at 6 and has not claimed, so is going for the iPhone. Exporter 224027 crossed 3 on 23 Sep and has not claimed AirPods; this is the referrer who opened the Polaroid popup on 4 Sep and backed out. Four people are one activation from AirPods. 19 of 68 Polaroid unlocks are claimed, every one at exactly one activation."}}